---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../../components/SiteFooter.astro";
import "../../styles/projects.css";
const report = "https://github.com/Nelson-Jnrnd/f1-pit-predictor-report";
---

<BaseLayout title="Pit-stop decision modelling · Nelson Jeanrenaud" description="My 2023 bachelor's thesis: preparing Formula 1 race data, comparing pit-stop prediction models, and examining their limitations.">
  <SiteHeader />
  <span id="top"></span>
  <main class="wrap project-detail">
    <section class="section">
      <a class="project-detail__back" href="/#projects">Back to projects</a>
      <p class="kicker">Academic project · B.Sc. thesis · 2023</p>
      <h1>Pit-stop decision modelling</h1>
      <p class="lead">Can historical race data help model when a Formula 1 team will pit and which tyres it will choose?</p>
      <p>I collected and prepared race data, compared machine-learning approaches, and examined their predictions and limitations. My thesis was graded 5.6/6. You can read my intermediate report below.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="data">
      <h2 id="data">The prediction task</h2>
      <p>I modelled two decisions: whether a car will pit, and which tyre compound it will use if it does. For the sequence-based model, I used previous laps to predict a stop on the following lap.</p>
      <p>I collected lap-by-lap race data using FastF1 and prepared inputs such as tyre age, stint, lap time, track status and the gap to other drivers. I used historical team decisions as the target labels.</p>
      <h3>Models and evaluation</h3>
      <p>I compared random forests, neural networks and recurrent neural networks. I trained the models on races from 2019–2022 and reserved 2023 for testing. I separated the training and validation data before preprocessing to avoid information leaking between them.</p>
      <p>Pit stops are rare compared with laps without a stop. I examined precision, recall and F1 scores rather than relying on overall accuracy, alongside charts showing predicted pit-stop probabilities throughout a race and explanations of individual predictions.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="finding">
      <h2 id="finding">Results and limitations</h2>
      <figure class="project-evidence">
        <a href="/projects/pit-stop-probabilities-stroll-2023.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Open the pit-stop probability chart at full size">
          <img src="/projects/pit-stop-probabilities-stroll-2023.svg" alt="Predicted pit-stop probabilities over Lance Stroll's 2023 Spanish Grand Prix. Red vertical lines mark the prediction targets one lap before actual stops; the upper bars show tyre compounds." width="1067" height="480" loading="lazy" />
        </a>
        <figcaption>A figure from my thesis: Lance Stroll, Spain 2023. Predictions use the preceding lap; red markers show the target one lap before each actual pit stop.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <p>In this example, the random-forest probabilities increased during a stint and fell after a stop, with a slower increase on hard tyres. I identified tyre age, lap number and stint among the important inputs. My models still produced many false positive pit-stop predictions.</p>
      <p>My models learned to imitate historical decisions, which does not establish an optimal strategy. They captured relationships in race data but still struggled to pinpoint the stopping lap. I therefore treated their probabilities as signals to examine rather than proof that a stop was the best decision.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="sources">
      <h2 id="sources">Report and code</h2>
      <ul class="project-detail__sources">
        <li><a href={`${report}/blob/master/report.pdf`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public intermediate report (French PDF)</a></li>
        <li><a href={`${report}/blob/master/experience.tex`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Experiment descriptions and results</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://github.com/Nelson-Jnrnd/f1-pit-predictor-dataset" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Race-data collection repository</a></li>
        <li><a href="/projects/formula-one-analysis">Related personal work: Formula 1 telemetry analysis</a></li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</BaseLayout>
